     =20
        USE OF RECEIPTS/INVOICES:=20
        <br><br>
       =20
     =20
        <b>Before you can start your business operations, please ensure =
that your Invoices are printed and ready for use in all sales transactions.=
 </b>
        <br><br>
        Your options: <br><br>
     =20
        1.	Have your own Invoices printed <br>
        <br><br>
       =20
     =20
        <b>Apply for Authority to Print (ATP). Submit Final clear =
sample of Invoices and/or Supplementary Document to the RDO where you are =
registered or=20
        through ORUS by accessing the Secondary =
Registration functionality.</b>
     =20
        <br><br>
     =20
        2.	Buy BIR Printed Invoices (BPI) in the RDO where you are =
registered. <br>
     =20
        BPI can be used within the first year of =
business or until its full consumption, whichever comes first. <br>
     =20
        Taxpayer is required to secure ATP principal =
receipts/invoices and have its own invoices printed beginning its second =
(2nd) year of its operations. <br>
      <br><br>
       =20
     =20
        <b>Failure or refusal to issue receipts or sales or commercial =
invoices, shall, upon conviction for each act or omission, is punishable by=
 a fine of not less than One Thousand Pesos (Php 1,000.00) but not more =
than Fifty Thousand Pesos (Php 50,000.00) and suffer imprisonment of not =
less than two (2) years but not more than four (4) years, pursuant to =
Section 264 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC) of 1997, as =
amended. </b>
      <br><br>
       =20
     =20
        <b> REGISTRATION =
OF MANUAL BOOKS OF ACCOUNTS </b>
      <br><br>
        New Sets of Manual =
Books of Accounts must be registered before use. Online registration of =
Books of Accounts is available in ORUS.
      <br><br>
       =20
     =20
        <b> ATTEND TAXPAYER BRIEFING </b>
      <br><br>
        You must attend Taxpayer Briefing being conducted by your RDO for =
more tax information on your tax compliance. You may check the regular tax =
briefing schedule for new business registrants in your respective RDOs by =
visiting our BIR website at www.bir.gov.ph.
      <br><br>
       =20
     =20
        <b> POSTING OF BIR CERTIFICATE OF REGISTRATION </b>
      <br><br>
        The Electronic Certificate of Registration must be =
printed and should be posted or exhibited at the principal place of =
business and at each branch or through its ecommerce website or online =
store in case of persons engaged in online business or activity, in a way =
that is clearly and easily visible to the public.=20
      <br><br>
       =20
      <br><br>
        <b> POSTING OF NOTICE TO ISSUE INVOICES =
(NII) </b>
      <br><br>
        The Notice to issue Invoice (NII) is =
required to be posted conspicuously in the place of business including =
branches and mobile stores. Taxpayers can get NII at the RDO where they are=
 registered.
      <br><br>
       =20
     =20
        <b> =
TAXPAYER=E2=80=99S GUIDE </b>
      <br><br>
        You may download the =
applicable taxpayer guide for your reference from the BIR Website (www.bir.=
gov.ph).

      <br><br>
       =20
        <b> CHANGE IN REGISTRATION =
INFORMATION </b>
      <br><br>
        For any change in registration =
information with the BIR, taxpayer must update its record with the BIR =
through ORUS or by submitting BIR Form No. 1905 to the RDO where the =
taxpayer is registered.
